    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n59" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăbĕcĕdārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um
		a, b, c, d, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>belonging to the alphabet, alphabetical</i> (late
			Lat.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">psalmi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Retract. 1, 20</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b><i>Subst</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăbĕcĕdāĭus</span></b> ,
				ĭi, m., <i>one
				who learns the a, b, c</i> (eccl. Lat.).
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăbĕcĕdārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>elementary
				instruction</i>, <i><span class="en">Fulg. Myth. 3,
			10</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăbĕ-cĕdārĭum</span></b> ,
				ĭi, n., <i>a,
				b, c, the alphabet</i> (eccl. Lat.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
